The [[Falcon Blade]] is a neutral [[Weapon]] normally obtained by combining a [[Hero Sword]] with two [[Gloves of Haste]]. It deals moderate damage overall, and attacks twice, which can be useful for {{icon/vampirism}} builds, but could cause problems against large amounts of {{icon/spikes}}. It also massively speeds up any items near it, which is especially good with items that don't consume stamina.

The player can play into it attacking twice as a strength as [[Gemstone|gemstones]] will essentially get doubled value, and effects that increase the '''Falcon Blade's''' base damage make it very powerful. [[Djinn Lamp|Djinn Lamps]] can make this item very powerful in the right build, and each activation of the '''Falcon Blade''' essentially counts as two activations, which makes it excellent for gaining {{icon/mana}} from the [[Mana Orb]]. This synergy can make [[Mana Mastery]] + Mana Orb builds with '''Falcon Blade''' and potentially a few Djinn Lamps powerful.

However, because it attacks twice per attack, it will interact with [[Shield|Shields]] twice as well, which can make it relatively weak against builds with one or several shields. Despite attacking twice, the item will only use [[Stamina]] once. As long as the player has enough stamina to attack, both hits will occur. Shields will have a separate chance to interact with both of the Blade's hits, potentially blocking one, both, or neither.

By combining the [[Falcon Blade]] with the [[Hero Longsword]]s, the [[Crossblades]] can be created, which is a powerful +-shaped weapon which grants a large amount of damage to one weapon and massively speeds up another item. It also deals more damage and attacks faster with every hit.
